  "id": "0b4f9f90-b0b8-5e95-9b12-39e58f213097",
  "slug": "pink-velvet-cake-recipe-8637225",
  "name": "Pink Velvet Cake",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "Give your standard boxed cake a fun and vibrant spin with this Pink Velvet Cake recipe. This light and lovely vanilla cake recipe uses buttermilk for flavor and tenderness, plus a touch of pink to give it a vibrant color. Here\u2019s how to make Pink Velvet Cake.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Lightly coat a 9x13-inch baking pan with baking spray; set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Whisk together cake mix, buttermilk, oil, eggs, and food coloring in a medium bowl until fully combined and no dry streaks remain. Transfer to the prepared baking pan and spread in an even layer."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until a wooden pick inserted in center comes out clean, 20 to 25 minutes. Let cool completely in pan on a wire rack, about 1 hour."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Beat cream cheese and butter with an electric mixer on medium speed until light and fluffy, 1 to 2 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Gradually beat in powdered sugar with mixer on low speed, until smooth and fully combined, stopping to scrape down sides of bowl as needed, about 3 minutes. Add vanilla and salt and beat until just combined."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Using an offset spatula, spread cream cheese frosting evenly over the top of the cooled cake. Garnish with sprinkles, if desired."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Cut into squares and serve. Recipe developed by Amanda Holstein"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 12,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 20,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 20,
